Hey Robin,

For sure, as a Lojban newbie, I'm skating on thin ice here...

But I can see a lot of mechanisms in Lojban where, if they were removed, th=
en the language would be highly difficult to use for informal communication=
.

On the other hand, natural languages are really redundant -- you could remo=
ve a LOT of mechanisms from a natural language and it would still be practi=
cally usable, because there are so many workarounds...

With Lojban, clearly there are no (or hardly any) mechanisms that could be =
removed and still leave the language usable.....=20=20

And my guess is that there are a few mechanisms that will still be added to=
 Lojban in the future to make the language more usable (though given my rel=
ative ignorance I hesitate to suggest what these might be at this stage...)

It seems like it has been a lot of work to add enough mechanisms to Lojban =
to make it usable without sacrificing the spirit of the language..

-- Ben


